%% Capture (J-001): proposals are confirmed in the Claude Code conversation; the capture server validates before writing.
%% Pictogram and illustration are optional: the author may decline either, and the concept is saved without it (FR-034, FR-035, PD-026).
sequenceDiagram
  actor Author
  participant CC as Claude Code
  participant Cap as Capture server (MCP, stdio)
  participant Store as Concept files

  Author->>CC: Capture "Secure cookie attribute"
  CC->>Cap: list_concepts
  Cap->>Store: read frontmatter of all concepts
  Cap-->>CC: ids, titles, layers, pictograms, pictogram catalog
  CC-->>Author: proposed relations with sources, SEE-I draft, layer and facets
  Author->>CC: keep relations, write one explanation each, accept or rewrite each SEE-I part
  CC-->>Author: proposed pictogram from the catalog
  Author->>CC: accept, ask for another, or decline
  opt illustration part is drawable (FR-035)
    CC->>Cap: preview_illustration(id, illustration)
    alt SVG passes the allowlist
      Cap-->>CC: preview page path (temp page outside the store, opened in the default browser as an image)
      CC-->>Author: proposed visual illustration shown in the browser
      Author->>CC: accept, ask for another, or decline
    else SVG fails the allowlist
      Cap-->>CC: rejected: invalid_illustration with the reasons
      CC-->>Author: draws another illustration
    end
  end
  CC-->>Author: proposed recall questions
  Author->>CC: confirm questions, name the episode
  CC->>Cap: save_concept(concept, accepted pictogram and illustration if any)
  alt every rule holds (BR-001 to BR-005)
    Cap->>Store: write illustration SVG first when present, then the concept file (temp file, rename into place)
    Cap-->>CC: saved
    CC-->>Author: saved, first review due tomorrow
  else a rule fails (including unknown pictogram or invalid illustration)
    Cap-->>CC: rejected: the exact field or relation (UX-003)
    CC-->>Author: what to fix
  end
